NX-Nexus — licensing and third-party attributions
=================================================

NX-Nexus is licensed **GPL-3.0-or-later**. See LICENSE for the full text.

The licence was chosen deliberately, not by default. GPL-3.0 is the only
licence under which the whole intended component set can lawfully be combined:

  - Goldleaf and nxdumptool are GPL-3.0-or-later (verified from their own
    per-file headers). Their copyleft requires any work derived from them to be
    GPL-3.0-compatible.
  - libusbhsfs's full-featured build is GPLv2-or-later, which the "or later"
    clause allows to be combined under GPL-3.0.
  - mtp-server-nx is Apache-2.0. Apache-2.0 is compatible with **GPLv3 but not
    GPLv2**, because of its patent and notice terms. This is the specific
    reason the project is GPLv3 rather than GPLv2.
  - libnx (ISC) and Dear ImGui (MIT) are permissive and impose no constraint.

See docs/PLAN-REVIEW.md §1 for the full reasoning and the alternatives that
were rejected.


