The one thing no licence choice can fix
---------------------------------------

The original blueprint listed "Huntereb/Tinwoo" as a source for PFS0 and NCA
handling. That repository does not exist, and the surviving forks
(falcorr/TinWoo, daz2048/TinWoo) declare **no licence at all**.

No licence means no grant of rights. Unlike the GPL projects, this is not
solved by relicensing NX-Nexus — there is simply no permission to copy that
code under any terms. Tinwoo must not be used as a source, and its absence is
the reason Phase 2's PFS0/NCA work still has to come from either the switchbrew
wiki or from Goldleaf/nxdumptool (both now permissible).


