Derived work currently in this repository
-----------------------------------------

src/usb/usb_transport.c
  The usb:ds initialisation sequence — string and device descriptor setup, the
  per-speed AppendConfigurationData ordering, SuperSpeed companion descriptor
  placement, derivation of endpoint addresses from the interface index, and the
  PostBufferAsync / CompletionEvent / GetReportData / ParseReportData transfer
  cycle — follows the reference implementation in libnx's
  nx/source/runtime/devices/usb_comms.c (ISC License, switchbrew/libnx),
  retargeted from the vendor-specific class to the USB Still Image class.

  ISC is permissive; this attribution satisfies it, and the file is
  redistributed here as part of a GPL-3.0-or-later work.

include/nexus/mtp_types.h
  MTP and PTP protocol constants transcribed from the public PIMA 15740:2000
  specification and Microsoft's published MTP extension. Protocol numbers are
  facts about a wire format, not copyrightable expression.

src/horizon/fs_ext.c
  nexusFsOpenGameCardStorage is ported from nxdumptool's source/core/fs_ext.c
  (Copyright DarkMatterCore and contributors, GPL-3.0-or-later). libnx wraps
  fsOpenGameCardFileSystem but not the raw-sector fsp-srv command 30, which is
  what a byte-exact XCI dump requires.

  Modified 2026-09-03: renamed to nexusFsOpenGameCardStorage to carry this
  project's prefix, and the partition argument given a named enum. The IPC
  itself is unchanged.

src/horizon/sysinfo.c
  The Exosphere SPL configuration item used to detect an emuMMC boot
  (item 65007, ExosphereEmummcType) was identified from nxdumptool's
  source/core/nxdt_utils.c (GPL-3.0-or-later). The surrounding code is
  original.

src/horizon/compat.c
  Item 65000, ExosphereApiVersion, from the same Exosphere ABI and identified
  the same way. The surrounding code is original.

src/format/ncz.c, src/installer/ncz_decode.c
  The NCZ container layout — the "NCZSECTN" preamble at 0x4000, the 0x38-byte
  section entry, the AES-CTR counter construction, and the fact that the first
  0x4000 bytes are the original NCA header copied through — was taken from the
  format documentation and the reference decompressor published by nicoboss:

    https://github.com/nicoboss/nsz
    nsz/IndependentNczDecompressorConcise.py, docs/formats.md

  This is a clean-room implementation in C from that description. No code was
  copied; the reference is Python and was consulted for the layout only. It was
  consulted in preference to docs/formats.md alone because the prose there
  folds the one-off section magic into the section entry, which reads as though
  entries were 0x48 bytes rather than 0x38.

  Worth recording for anyone auditing the no-keys claim: an NCZ carries the AES
  key and counter for each section in its own header, deliberately, so that
  third-party installers can rebuild the NCA without deriving key material.
  Creating an NSZ requires prod.keys; installing one does not, and NX-Nexus
  holds no key material of its own.

src/installer/firmware.c
  Clean-room from the switchbrew wiki. Atmosphere's Daybreak was NOT used as a
  source: Atmosphere is GPL-2.0-**only** ("version 2, as published by the Free
  Software Foundation", with no "or later" clause), which is incompatible with
  this project's GPL-3.0-or-later. This is the one project in the ecosystem
  that the GPLv3 choice makes unavailable.

Everything else in this repository is original work by the NX-Nexus
contributors. Nothing has been copied from Goldleaf, libusbhsfs or
mtp-server-nx. Goldleaf's NSP installer was read to confirm that the Meta NCA's
own content info has to be constructed by hand rather than read from the CNMT,
but no code was taken from it.


Recording future imports
------------------------

When code is imported from any of the now-permissible upstreams:

  1. Keep the original file's copyright and licence header intact. Do not
     replace an upstream author's notice with a NX-Nexus one.
  2. For Apache-2.0 files (mtp-server-nx), retain the Apache notices and any
     NOTICE content the upstream ships; Apache-2.0 files stay Apache-2.0 inside
     the GPLv3 combined work rather than being relabelled.
  3. Add an entry to this file naming the upstream project, the files taken,
     and the upstream licence.
  4. Note any modifications, as GPL section 5(a) requires modified files to
     carry prominent notice of the change and its date.
